{%- comment -%}
  APEX ambassador program page.

  Three bands: greyscale photographic banner, the program explained beside the
  offer card, one closing CTA. The card is set exactly as
  `.facility-subs__card` — bronze-washed panel, tier name and dot on a head
  row, an oversized figure, then a checked list.

  WHAT DIFFERS FROM THE FACILITY CARD, AND WHY
  It carries two lists, not one. Three of the five program points are things
  an ambassador RECEIVES; two are things they are ASKED FOR (the $300-$800
  monthly target and the 90-120 day review). Setting the asks under the same
  bronze check as the perks would read as a benefit, which they are not, so
  they sit in their own group behind a bronze dash.

  COPY IS DRAFTED, NOT SUPPLIED
  There was no mockup for this page. The defaults below are written to the
  program summary given in chat and claim nothing beyond it — no payout
  schedule, no deadline, no ambassador count, no tier names. Every number on
  the page (10-pack, 10% off, 10% commission, 90-120 days, $300-$800) traces
  back to that summary, and the copy says plainly that Apex sells one ball
  and nothing else.

  THE APPLY LINK IS ONE SETTING, USED IN THREE PLACES
  The hero button, the offer card button and the closing CTA all read
  `apply_url`, which now points at the UpPromote affiliate sign-up. Repointing
  the whole page is one setting change, not three.

  `login_url` is the one link that deliberately does NOT follow it — a
  returning affiliate is signing in, not applying.

  NO BLOCKS. Everything on the page is a section setting — there is no
  repeating element left to make a block out of.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign apply_url = section.settings.apply_url | default: '/pages/contact'

  assign gets = section.settings.card_features | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
  assign asks = section.settings.card_expectations | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
-%}

<div
  class="amb"
  style="
    --amb-bg: {{ section.settings.background }};
    --amb-pad: {{ section.settings.padding_block }}px;
    --amb-hero-opacity: {{ section.settings.hero_image_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --amb-hero-gray: {{ section.settings.hero_greyscale | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --amb-hero-focus: {{ section.settings.hero_focus_x }}% {{ section.settings.hero_focus_y }}%;
    --amb-tone-strength: {{ section.settings.card_tone_strength }}%;
  "
>
  {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------------- Banner {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="amb-hero">
    {%- if section.settings.hero_image != blank -%}
      {{
        section.settings.hero_image
        | image_url: width: 1500
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'eager',
          fetchpriority: 'high',
          sizes: '100vw',
          widths: '480, 768, 1000, 1200, 1500',
          class: 'amb-hero__media',
          alt: ''
      }}
    {%- elsif section.settings.fallback_image_name != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Falls back to a file uploaded under Content > Files. A filename carries
        no intrinsic dimensions, so the width/height pair is the source frame
        rather than a measurement — it only reserves a box before CSS lands.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <img
        class="amb-hero__media"
        src="{{ section.settings.fallback_image_name | file_url }}"
        alt=""
        width="1500"
        height="1000"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      >
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="amb-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="apex-container amb-hero__inner">
      <h1 class="amb-hero__heading">
        {{ section.settings.hero_heading | escape }}
        {%- if section.settings.hero_heading_accent != blank -%}
          <span class="amb-accent">{{ section.settings.hero_heading_accent | escape }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </h1>

      {%- if section.settings.hero_text != blank -%}
        <p class="amb-hero__text">{{ section.settings.hero_text | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.hero_cta_label != blank -%}
        <div class="amb-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-light" href="{{ apply_url }}">
            {{ section.settings.hero_cta_label | escape }}
          </a>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ------------------------------- The program + the offer {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="amb-band" aria-labelledby="amb-intro">
    <div class="apex-container amb-offer">
      <div class="amb-offer__copy">
        {%- if section.settings.intro_heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="amb-h2" id="amb-intro">{{ section.settings.intro_heading | escape }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.intro_text != blank -%}
          <div class="amb-rte">{{ section.settings.intro_text }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Returning affiliates. This is the ONLY link on the page that does not
          go to `apply_url` — everything else is an application, this is a
          sign-in for someone who already applied, so it is deliberately a
          quiet arrow link rather than a fourth button competing with them.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Gated on the URL, not the copy. Shopify's `url` setting type refuses
          a schema `default`, so the link is only ever set from the template —
          and "Already have an affiliate login account?" with nothing to click
          is worse than no line at all.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.login_url != blank -%}
          <p class="amb-login">
            {%- if section.settings.login_text != blank -%}
              <span class="amb-login__text">{{ section.settings.login_text | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <a class="btn btn-link" href="{{ section.settings.login_url }}">
              {{ section.settings.login_label | default: 'Log in here' | escape }}
              {% render 'icon-arrow-right' %}
            </a>
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="amb-card">
        {%- if section.settings.card_badge != blank -%}
          <span class="amb-card__badge">{{ section.settings.card_badge | escape }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="amb-card__head">
          <span class="amb-card__tier">{{ section.settings.card_tier | escape }}</span>
          <span class="amb-card__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>

        {%- if section.settings.card_figure != blank -%}
          <p class="amb-card__figure">
            <span class="amb-card__figure-amount">{{ section.settings.card_figure | escape }}</span>
            {%- if section.settings.card_figure_suffix != blank -%}
              <span class="amb-card__figure-suffix">{{ section.settings.card_figure_suffix | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.card_description != blank -%}
          <p class="amb-card__description">{{ section.settings.card_description | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.card_features != blank -%}
          <div class="amb-card__group">
            {%- if section.settings.card_features_label != blank -%}
              <p class="amb-card__group-label">{{ section.settings.card_features_label | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <ul class="amb-card__list" role="list">
              {%- for item in gets -%}
                {%- assign item_text = item | strip -%}
                {%- if item_text != blank -%}
                  <li class="amb-card__row">
                    {% render 'svg-icons', icon: 'check-circle', class: 'amb-card__check' %}
                    <span>{{ item_text | escape }}</span>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.card_expectations != blank -%}
          <div class="amb-card__group">
            {%- if section.settings.card_expectations_label != blank -%}
              <p class="amb-card__group-label">{{ section.settings.card_expectations_label | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <ul class="amb-card__list" role="list">
              {%- for item in asks -%}
                {%- assign item_text = item | strip -%}
                {%- if item_text != blank -%}
                  <li class="amb-card__row">
                    <span class="amb-card__dash" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span>{{ item_text | escape }}</span>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.card_cta_label != blank -%}
          <a class="btn btn-outline btn-full amb-card__cta" href="{{ apply_url }}">
            {{ section.settings.card_cta_label | escape }}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} --------------------------------------------- Closing CTA {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.cta_heading != blank -%}
    <section class="amb-band amb-band--cta">
      <div class="apex-container amb-cta">
        <h2 class="amb-h2">{{ section.settings.cta_heading | escape }}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.cta_text != blank -%}
          <p class="amb-cta__text">{{ section.settings.cta_text | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
          <a class="btn btn-light" href="{{ apply_url }}">{{ section.settings.cta_label | escape }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* ==========================================================================
     APEX ambassador program.

     Every band on this page is dark, so there is no ink-flip layer here as
     there is on the two partner pages — type reads the palette tokens
     directly. If a light or bronze band is ever added back, that indirection
     comes back with it.

     MOBILE FIRST. Everything above the media queries is the phone layout.
     ========================================================================== */

  .amb {
    background-color: var(--amb-bg, var(--color-bg));
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }

  /* --- shared type -------------------------------------------------------- */

  .amb-h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: var(--weight-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    line-height: var(--leading-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-wrap: balance;
    /* A 48px heading in a 390px viewport has no room to lose. Without this a
       single long word (AMBASSADOR is 11 characters) overhangs the gutter
       instead of breaking. */
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .amb-accent {
    color: var(--brand-accent);
  }

  .amb-rte {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  .amb-rte > :first-child { margin-block-start: 0; }
  .amb-rte > :last-child { margin-block-end: 0; }

  .amb-rte strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  }

  /* Sits between the intro copy and the offer card, so it takes the copy's
     measure rather than the band's — a returning affiliate should find it
     where they stopped reading. Wraps to two lines on a narrow viewport with
     the link keeping its own baseline. */
  .amb-login {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  .amb-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
  }

  /* --- bands -------------------------------------------------------------- */

  .amb-band {
    padding-block: var(--amb-pad, var(--space-section));
  }

  /* The closing CTA is the highest band on the page, not a bronze one.

     A bronze ground was the obvious echo of the partner pages, but theirs
     carries a pull-quote at display size. This band carries a paragraph at
     --text-lead, and the darkest ink available on #A56D36 tops out around
     4.1:1 — under AA for text that size, and there is nothing darker than
     --ground to reach for. Bronze stays where it belongs here: the rule above
     the band, and the CTA's own hover fill. */
  .amb-band--cta {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border-block-start: var(--rule-thickness) solid var(--brand-accent);
  }

  /* --- banner -------------------------------------------------------------
     The header overlays this section, so the top padding clears
     --header-height before any copy starts. svh, not vh, so a mobile
     browser's collapsing address bar does not resize the banner mid-scroll. */

  .amb-hero {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    min-height: min(50rem, 82svh);
    padding-block: calc(var(--header-height) + var(--space-md)) var(--space-xl);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-deep);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .amb-hero__media {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    /* A group shot loses people at the frame edge when a 3:2 source is cropped
       to a portrait banner. The focal point is a setting for exactly that. */
    object-position: var(--amb-hero-focus, 50% 50%);
    opacity: var(--amb-hero-opacity, 0.55);
    /* Greyscale is the point, not a stylistic accident — it is what keeps a
       full-colour outdoor photograph from fighting the bronze accent sitting
       on top of it. Contrast is nudged back up because desaturating a warm
       image flattens it. */
    filter: grayscale(var(--amb-hero-gray, 1)) contrast(1.08);
  }

  .amb-hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground) 74%, transparent) 0%,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground) 30%, transparent) 38%,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground) 94%, transparent) 100%
    );
  }

  .amb-hero__inner {
    position: relative;
  }

  .amb-hero__heading {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    line-height: var(--leading-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-wrap: balance;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  /* The accent half of the headline drops to its own line rather than running
     on. Two colours in one wrapped paragraph read as an error; two colours on
     two lines read as a deliberate second beat. */
  .amb-accent {
    display: block;
  }

  .amb-hero__text {
    margin: var(--space-sm) 0 0;
    max-width: 54ch;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  /* --- the program + the offer --------------------------------------------
     One card, so it is paired with the copy rather than left alone in a row
     of three. Below 990 the copy stacks above it, full width. */

  .amb-offer {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* Bronze wash mixed against `transparent`, not against the band colour, so
     the card carries its own alpha and stays correct if the band background
     is ever re-pointed in the editor. */
  .amb-card {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--brand-accent-dim);
    background-color: color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--brand-accent) var(--amb-tone-strength, 7%),
      transparent
    );
  }

  .amb-card__badge {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: calc(var(--space-sm) * -0.5);
    inset-inline-start: var(--space-sm);
    padding: var(--space-unit) var(--space-2xs);
    background-color: var(--brand-accent);
    color: var(--color-text-on-light);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .amb-card__head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .amb-card__tier {
    color: var(--brand-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-eyebrow);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .amb-card__dot {
    flex: none;
    width: 1.2rem;
    height: 1.2rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: var(--brand-accent);
  }

  .amb-card__figure {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Amount and suffix stack rather than sharing a baseline. The suffix here is
     a full clause, not a "/mo" — inline it would be an unbreakable run beside
     a 36px figure. */
  .amb-card__figure-amount {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    font-weight: var(--weight-display);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .amb-card__figure-suffix {
    display: block;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xs);
    max-width: 32ch;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .amb-card__description {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  .amb-card__group {
    padding-block-start: var(--space-sm);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .amb-card__group-label {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-eyebrow);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: var(--weight-eyebrow);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-eyebrow);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .amb-card__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .amb-card__row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .amb-card__check {
    flex: none;
    width: 1.6rem;
    height: 1.6rem;
    margin-block-start: 0.1rem;
    color: var(--brand-accent);
  }

  /* The asks get a bronze dash, not a check. A check next to "hit $300-$800 a
     month" would read as something already granted. Sized and offset to sit on
     the same optical line the check icon occupies. */
  .amb-card__dash {
    flex: none;
    width: 1.6rem;
    height: var(--rule-thickness);
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
    background-color: var(--brand-accent);
  }

  .amb-card__cta {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  /* --- closing CTA --------------------------------------------------------- */

  .amb-cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .amb-cta__text {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 52ch;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  /* --- tablet -------------------------------------------------------------- */

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .amb-card {
      padding: var(--space-md);
    }

    .amb-card__badge {
      inset-inline-start: var(--space-md);
    }
  }

  /* --- desktop -------------------------------------------------------------
     The offer becomes two columns here rather than at 750: the card's own
     content (a 56px figure plus two labelled lists) needs ~380px before the
     copy beside it has anywhere to go, and at 750 the rail is only ~654px. */

  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    .amb-offer {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr minmax(38rem, 46rem);
      gap: var(--grid-gap);
    }

    .amb-cta {
      flex-direction: row;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: var(--space-lg);
    }

    .amb-cta .amb-h2 {
      flex: 1 1 40rem;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "APEX ambassadors",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "apex-ambassadors-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Banner"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "hero_image",
      "label": "Banner image",
      "info": "Rendered greyscale behind the headline. Recommended 1500px wide or more. Falls back to the file named below if empty."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "fallback_image_name",
      "label": "Fallback file name",
      "info": "A file uploaded under Content > Files. Used only when no banner image is picked above.",
      "default": "Project_20260813_0255.jpg"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hero_greyscale",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Greyscale",
      "info": "100% is fully desaturated, which is what keeps the photograph from fighting the bronze accent.",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hero_image_opacity",
      "min": 15,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Image strength",
      "default": 55
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hero_focus_x",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Focal point, horizontal",
      "info": "Which part of the photograph stays in frame when it is cropped to the banner.",
      "default": 50
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hero_focus_y",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Focal point, vertical",
      "default": 40
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Every court has someone people listen to."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_heading_accent",
      "label": "Heading, accent line",
      "info": "Set in bronze on its own line.",
      "default": "Be ours."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "hero_text",
      "label": "Supporting copy",
      "default": "We make one thing — the Apex 48. Ambassadors are the players who put it in other people's hands: a bag of balls every month to share, a code of your own, and 10% of everything it brings in."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_cta_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "Apply to be an ambassador"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Apply link"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "apply_url",
      "label": "Apply link",
      "info": "Used by all three apply buttons on this page — hero, offer card and closing CTA. Points at the UpPromote affiliate sign-up."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "What it means"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "intro_heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "What it means to be an Apex ambassador."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "intro_text",
      "label": "Body",
